All this talk of cockatrice eggs got me thinking (a dangerous
activity).

Would not a cockatrice egg have a very interesting effect when used as
a hand grenade?

And now for something completely different....

Much labor got me a compile for NH3.0i on the Amiga.  I used the Aztec
C 5.0d so I got the 68020 code in there for a little speed, plus I have
enough memory to use ALL the options.

This is harder than you think, since the code had been ZIP'ed on an IBM
PC compatible.  There were jillions of little "^M's" in the source
(only causes problems in some #defines), and the file names were
changed to make them shorter.  I always knew there was a reason those
machines made me uncomfortable....  Aside from that, you should SEE
what I did to that poor innocent makefile.

Reading a fortune cookie always prints a blank message.  I did change
the names for the fortunes files, so I'm pretty sure they're correct
now.  I'm under the vague impression that the message gets printed on
the screen and then erased, but I could be imagining it....

The above is merely an annoyance, since I read the fortunes files
anyway (so, sue me).  HOWEVER, the save/restore sequence is a little
weird.  It seems to work ok.  However, the names of everything get
messed up on the restore.  It looks like the pointers are in the wrong
places.  This naturally leads to a few unprintable characters getting
sent to the screen, leading to a few unprintable words from myself.
The objects in my inventory seem to perform normally, but their names
are munged, so I can't tell what I've got.  Since the Amiga is
multitasking, I could simply leave the computer going, but then I don't
have any memory to work with, and I don't feel like forking over the
money for the memory just now.....

I also have not been able to get the custom font to work.  The docs are
very unclear on this.  Can anybody find/give me a step-by-step on what
you need to do to install/use the custom font?  I gave up and switched
back to the normal font.

If nobody has good solutions to the first two issues, I might be able
to tolerate a pre-compiled 68000 version, if someone assured me that it
was compiled with ALL the options before I download it.  It's just nice
when the 68030 can use the special instructions for a little more
speed....

